  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string SSS consisting of only ((( and ))).\n\nFind the length of the **longest** substring of SSS which is a valid parentheses string.\n\nNote:\n\n\nA substring of a string is obtained by deleting some (possibly zero) characters from the beginning and some (possibly zero) characters from the end.\nA valid parentheses string is defined as:\n\nEmpty string is valid.\nIf PPP is valid, (P)(P)(P) is also valid.\nIf PPP and QQQ are valid, PQPQPQ is also valid.\n\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case consists of a string SSS, consisting of ((( and ))) only.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the length of the **longest** substring of SSS which is a valid parentheses string.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤20001 \\leq T \\leq 20001≤T≤2000",
      "1≤∣S∣≤1051 \\leq |S| \\leq 10^51≤∣S∣≤105",
      "SSS contains ((( and ))) only.",
      "The sum of ∣S∣|S|∣S∣ over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n(()\n)\n)(())()\n)((",
        "output": "2\n0\n6\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The longest valid parentheses substring is ()()() having length 222.\nTest case 222: There is no valid parentheses substring in the string.\nTest case 333: The longest valid parentheses substring is (())()(())()(())() having length 666.\nTest case 444: There is no valid parentheses substring in the string."
      }
    ]
  },
